our next attack now the head of the  hammer is also not solid it's got these  holes for the fire to burst through upon  contact so that's my theory on this  weapon moving on we have what I'm going  to call the scythe cleaver  and  call it that because it's a mixture of  the scythe and the very standard saw  cleaver weapons now the shortened form  is similar to the common saw cleaver  except without the serrated blade and it  extends to this simple straighter scythe  than the one the way used to it appears  twice in the trailer with a similar move  set to the saw cleaver and the saw spear  weapons they currently exist so it's  pretty standard and kind of boring and  the next weapon though oh boy this looks  awesome it's a bow in blood-borne where  we have guns but I'm gonna use the bow  anyway it's amazing and if the DLC  blogpost is to be believed it's  technically a bow blade they call it  simon's bow blade and from the visuals  it's most logical to assume that the bow  sort of folds together to form a twisted  sort of sword or perhaps it's another  dual wielding weapon now since a bow has  a really bent structure it's possible  that it transforms into a twisted sword  and there is a twisted sword later in  the trailer but the shapes of the sword  and the bow are quite different so while  I initially thought they might transform  together they do seem distinct from one  another this twisted sword is  represented alongside a shield and it's  a shield that isn't just a plank of wood  which is nice next we have what I'm  going to call the chain cleaver I'm just  pointing phrases left and right here  it's move set is similar to the threaded  cane which extends like a whip when you  swing it but this weapons a little bit  different it looks significantly heavier  and more like a bludgeon type of weapon  and from a look at those solid metal  pieces here it looks as if the weapon  can be condensed down into more of a  bludgeon type of weapon here's what I  came up with after about 10 hours in  Photoshop that looks kinda legit next we  see a weapon that we're all familiar  with it's the Beast claws they're not  that great in the current game but it  looks almost like they are getting a  buff in the expansion so the character  here is performing a dive attack that  doesn't exist in the current game so how  does this attack come about well I  hypothesize that it's got something to  do with the character being more beast  like you look at the character here and  he has fur on  his back and his shoulder that extends  way more than it used to in the current  game so the Beast Clause was a weapon  that whenever you hit an enemy you get a  bit of beasts hood so maybe when your  beast hood meter is fuller you get  access to another move or something like  that I think it could be a clue that  beast hood is becoming a more developed  mechanic which is something a lot of  people have always wanted and I'd wager  that that's what you're looking at here  and finally we have this clip of a  hunter fighting the abhorrent beast in  the forbidden woods and his weapon in  its shortened form is this simple  one-handed pike you know like a spear  but the metal spike at the tip can  rotate perpendicularly and it can clip  to become a long pickaxe type of weapon  I'm gonna call it the pike axe and that  pretty much does it for weapons so let's  move on to attire and we'll go over it  pretty quick there's these three hunters  in the intro one of which is touting the  biggest hat we've seen since Dark Souls  1 there's a character you spot briefly  here on the right later in the trailer  wearing a red garb with puffy pants and  then the most curious outfit to me is  this one it's worn by the guy who's  wielding that circular saw blade and  look at that helmet it's like a metal  bucket does that look familiar  so story wise the dlc is said to be set  in a nightmare world where hunters from  the past are trapped forever the  playstation blog mentions that we 